d in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary node   are three pieces of fatty tissue which measure 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in aggregate  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal the presence of three candidate lymph nodes  Two lymph nodes are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  after being serially sectioned and inked red and blue  respectively  A single large lymph node is been serially sectioned  and submitted entirely in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Darryl A Oble M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Darryl A Oble M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   to strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals   REMOVED_CASE_ID   to chromosome 17 signals  156  in 60 tumor cell nuclei 