ed and verified the test s accuracy and precision Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  156  to chromosome 17 signals  137  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE  2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results   Lymphoma Workup RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STUDIES ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  Studies performed at MGH  The lymph node architecture is effaced by a proliferation of small lymphocytes  Scattered pale staining areas are seen containing larger cells  prolymphocytes  paraimmunoblasts   consistent with proliferation centers  With B lineage antibodies  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and PAX 5  there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and are negative for cyclin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Residual reactive follicles at the periphery of the lymph node are bcl6   With T lineage antibody  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of many small cells scattered within the tissue  A stain for Ki67 shows an appropriately high level of staining in reactive follicles  The lymphoma cells show a very low proliferation index   5    with slightly increased staining within proliferation centers  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of SMALL LYMPHOCYTIC LYMPHOMA  CONSISTENT WITH CHRONIC LYMPHOCYTIC LEUKEMIA  NOTE  Dr  Aliyah Rahemtullah has reviewed the lymph node specimens and concurs with the diagnosis of chronic lymphocytic leukemia small lymphocytic lymphoma  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  3 by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION PART E  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN   EXCISION PART F  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL DEEP MARGIN   EXCISION PART G  BREAST  report_end  , Negative.
