ned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE irregular  tan pink  gritty mass that is greater than 1 0cm from the deep margin  Several vague rubbery nodular areas are present adjacent to and away  up to  3 0cm from the mass  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest inferior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass and rubbery nodule adjacent to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fatty breast tissue away from tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Vague nodular area   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Rubbery nodule away from mass  An axillary node dissection is performed  and multiple nodes are identified  The largest node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  It is bisected  and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   An additional three nodes are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the remaining five nodes in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue   is a yellow red piece of soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The specimen is completely dissected to reveal multiple tiny lymph nodes  The largest is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  They are entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Miriam D Post M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined