Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  JAMES W MAY  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Frozen Section Resident  Gregor Krings  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results Reason for Addendum  3  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 43 year old woman undergoing a right mastectomy for extensive ductal carcinoma in situ with possible invasion  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  MULTIFOCAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  ARISING IN A BACKGROUND OF EXTENSIVE HIGH GRADE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   See table 1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  Multiple foci  Invasive carcinoma is present in multiple foci arising in association with a background of extensive high grade ductal carcinoma in situ  primarily located in the upper outer quadrant  The largest single focus of invasive tumor measures 0 6cm microscopically  The DCIS is present in 10 of 10 sections from the upper outer quadrant over an area measuring approximately 6 5cm  GRADE  3  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 1cm from the posterior margin along a broad front  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front  STAI